I immediately contacted the credit bureaus and submitted formal disputes, yet these inquiries remained without proper verification. I never signed a credit application or agreement permitting these entities to access my credit file. No application, loan, or account was opened as a result of these inquiries indicating there was no permissible purpose under the law. 

Laws Violated : These inquiries violate the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) in multiple sections : FCRA 604 ( a ) ( 3 ) A consumer report may only be furnished if there is a legitimate, permissible purpose, such as a credit application initiated by the consumer. 

FCRA 607 ( a ) Requires all entities that furnish data to credit bureaus to ensure they have proper procedures to ensure accuracy and compliance. 

FCRA 611 ( a ) Mandates the consumer reporting agency to conduct a reasonable reinvestigation if a consumer disputes any item on the report. 

