14193789,2025-06-20,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem accessing account,"( Revised for CFPB Submission No Personal Identifiers Included ) On XX/XX/year>, an issue arose with our account when a debit card was unexpectedly declined while attempting to pay for a meal. Upon attempting to log in, we received a message instructing us to contact Navy Federal. After calling the designated number, we were transferred to another department and informed that our account had been closed due to alleged fraud that we had "" participated in. '' We were told the decision was final and that no appeal process existed. This came as a complete shock, as we had received no prior contact or notification. 

The representative stated that the issue was related to XXXX activity. We rarely use XXXX and only to send money, never to receive it. At the representatives suggestion, we visited a local branch for clarification. There, we were told the problem involved XXXX deposits that had been made to our account. We never requested, authorized, or received such deposits. The only communication we had received were vague emails that appeared to be scam attempts, which we ignored. No unauthorized funds ever posted to our account. 

As longstanding members of Navy Federal with over 30 years of responsible financial historyincluding loans, savings, money market accounts, and bill paywe were stunned by the lack of communication and the abrupt closure of all accounts.

