14202473,2025-06-20,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Banking errors,"My identify was stolen XX/XX/XXXX. As part of this, I received fraudulent charges to my Wells Fargo checking account. The thief had deactivated my phone and enabled his, so he was able to receive my login confirmation codes, change passwords, and log into my financial institutions. Part of the fraudulent charges, were purchases to XXXX, some of which were ACH purchases. Despite closing my checking account and opening a new one, getting a new debit card, and placing a stop payment on all XXXX charges, the XXXX ACH transfers continued to the new checking account for the next few months, unbeknownst to me. This was a failure on Wells Fargos part. And because the fraudster used my phone number to buy himself XXXX, and presumably, pay for his monthly plan, Wells Fargo refuses to reimburse me for all of the charges, as they believe it was me making the purchases, because my phone number and checking account was used. But I dont and have never used XXXX XXXX Ive contacted XXXX and that was a dead end because I dont actually have an account with them. They wouldnt help me. You cant get ahold of a person. A local XXXX employee also tried to contact XXXX, with no success. I had filed a XXXX XXXX police report and did a report with the FTC, on XXXX. Wells Fargo refused to listen to me or give and credence to the whole identity theft case, despite my proof of my identity being stolen and will not reimburse me for all the fraudulent charges.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,WELLS FARGO & COMPANY,MT,59405,,Web,2025-06-20,Closed with explanation,Yes
