Applicable Legal Requirements : 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( a ) : Upon receiving appropriate proof of identity, a copy of an identity theft report, and a specific request, a credit reporting agency must block the reporting of information resulting from identity theft within 4 business days.

15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( c ) : A CRA may not refuse to block fraudulent information except under narrowly defined circumstances ( e.g., material misrepresentation or fraud by the consumer, neither of which applies in my case ).

15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) : A CRA must conduct a reasonable reinvestigation and delete unverifiable or inaccurate information within 30 days of a dispute.

15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) : You are required to follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy of the information in consumer reports. Continuing to report fraudulent accounts after receiving identity theft documentation fails to meet this standard.

Final Demand : I hereby demand : 1. Immediate deletion and blocking of the above-listed fraudulent accounts from my credit file.

2. A written statement confirming deletion and blocking of these accounts.

