14371454,2025-06-30,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing in reference to the response submitted by the furnisher in relation to my prior complaint ( # XXXX ). I respectfully dispute their claims and request that this case remain open for further investigation based on the following legal and procedural concerns : Insufficient Validation of Debt ( FDCPA 15 U.S. Code 1692g ) : The documentation provided by the furnisher does not constitute full validation under federal law. A mere copy of a contract and an account statement does not verify the complete chain of custody or prove that the alleged debt is valid, enforceable, and collectible. The FDCPA requires that they demonstrate their legal right to collect and furnish this debt, including : Proof of ownership or assignment of the debt A complete accounting of the debt from origination to present Confirmation that the balance is accurate and not inflated by unlawful fees or interest No Response to Specific Disputes under FCRA ( 15 U.S. Code 1681i ) : I had requested specific details challenging the accuracy of the information being reported to the Credit Reporting Agencies ( CRAs ). The furnisher did not provide any line-by-line verification or reinvestigation results as required under the FCRA. Simply claiming the debt is valid is not a substitute for a reinvestigation.

Material Omission Regarding Disputed Status ( FCRA 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 3 ) ) : While the furnisher claims they marked the account as disputed, I have obtained my credit report, and the disputed notation does not appear. This is a violation of their duty under the FCRA to report any account that is disputed by the consumer.

Failure to Provide Full Records of Communication and Transaction History : I formally requested all internal notes, call recordings, and communications pertaining to this account, along with a full payment history. To date, that information has not been provided. This omission prevents me from validating any alleged charges or interest accrued. 

License Status is Irrelevant Without Jurisdiction and Proof of Standing : While the company claims to be licensed in Ohio, they have failed to show jurisdiction, standing, or a legal right to collect this alleged debt in my state of residence, nor have they proven the debt is not time-barred under applicable statute of limitations laws.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,OH,43123,,Web,2025-06-30,Closed with explanation,Yes
