14372297,2025-06-30,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was result of identity theft,"I am filing this complaint because multiple personal loan accounts from Affirm Inc have been reported on my credit report, but I did not open or authorize any of these accounts. These accounts were opened without my knowledge or consent, and I believe I am a victim of identity theft. 

The accounts were : Opened in 2023 without my authorization. 
Reported as closed but still appear on my credit file. 
Not associated with any payment delinquencies, yet are contributing negatively to my credit profile. 

I have reached out to the credit bureaus and Affirm to request the removal of these accounts, but no resolution has been provided. These accounts are damaging my credit score and do not reflect my financial history.

Legal Grounds ( FCRA Citations ) : According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act : FCRA 611 [ 15 U.S. Code 1681i ] requires credit reporting agencies to conduct a reasonable investigation if a consumer disputes any item in their file. I formally disputed these accounts and provided evidence that they were opened fraudulently.

FCRA 605B [ 15 U.S. Code 1681c-2 ] entitles victims of identity theft to request that fraudulent information be blocked from appearing in their credit report. I submitted a fraud claim and supporting documents requesting that these accounts be permanently blocked.

FCRA 602 ( A ) emphasizes the need for consumer reporting agencies to adopt reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy. Continuing to report accounts that do not belong to me violates this obligation.",,"Affirm Holdings, Inc",GA,319XX,,Web,2025-06-30,Closed with explanation,Yes
